## 🔴 P0 — Critical (Release Blockers & Runtime Crashes)

### [x] T01: Fix Scoped Package Publishing Failure (HTTP 402)

- **Files:** [`package.json:2`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/package.json#L2), [`.github/workflows/publish.yml:34`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/.github/workflows/publish.yml#L34)
  \

\-][] **Problem:** Scoped packages (`@omid2007hope/*`) default to private access on npm. Without explicit public configuration, `npm publish` fails with `402 Payment Required`.

- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Add `"publishConfig": { "access": "public" }` to `package.json`.
  - [x] Add `run: npm publish --access public` to `.github/workflows/publish.yml`.

---

### [x] T02: Restore Full TypeScript Declarations in Distribution Bundle

- **Files:** [`package.json:25`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/package.json#L25), [`src/types/index.d.ts`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/types/index.d.ts), [`dist/index.d.ts:132`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/dist/index.d.ts#L132)
- **Problem:** `tsup` generates types from JavaScript files with incomplete JSDoc, overwriting `dist/index.d.ts` with `auto(..., any): any`. The handcrafted types in `src/types/index.d.ts` are dropped.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Update `src/types/index.d.ts`:
    - Allow `string` for `time` in `AutoRule` and `AutoVarRule` (e.g. `"18:30"`).
    - Declare `compile(rules: AutoRule[]): CompiledRules`.
    - Fix `autoVars` return type to `{ stop(): void }` and add `interval?: number`.
    - Support generic style payloads `<T = string | Record<string, string>>`.
  - [x] Ensure `tsup` build bundles or preserves the full type definitions from `src/types/index.d.ts`.

---

### [ ] T03: Prevent Unhandled Crashes on `null` Rules & Non-String Dates

- **Files:** [`src/core/engine.js:78-84`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/engine.js#L78-L84), [`src/core/utils.js:23-24`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/utils.js#L23-L24)
- **Problem:**
  - `compile()` crashes on `[condition && { time: 6 }]` when `condition` is falsy (`TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'vars')`).
  - `parseDate()` crashes with `str.split is not a function` if numbers or non-strings are provided.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Add guard in `compile()`: `if (!css || typeof css !== 'object') continue;`.
  - [x] Safely cast and validate strings in `parseDate()` before calling `.split('-')`.
  - [x] Add regression tests in `tests/bugfix.test.js`.

