## 🟠 P1 — High (Logic Flaws, Security / Stability Hazards & Framework Breakages)

### [ ] T04: Validate `parseTime` Ranges (Fix 24/7 Rule Takeover)

- **Files:** [`src/core/utils.js:106-123`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/utils.js#L106-L123), [`src/core/utils.js:133-145`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/utils.js#L133-L145)
- **Problem:** Times like `"25:00"` or `"99:99"` parse to minutes > 1439. In `getMatchingTimeRule`, wrap-around fallback promotes this invalid rule to be active 24 hours a day.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] In `parseTime()`, strictly validate that `h >= 0 && h <= 23 && m >= 0 && m <= 59`.
  - [x] Return `null` and log warning if time is out of valid bounds.
  - [x] Add unit test verifying invalid string times do not hijack the theme.

---

### [ ] T05: Fix Date + Time Composite Rule Wrap-Around Bug

- **Files:** [`src/core/engine.js:186-202`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/engine.js#L186-L202)
- **Problem:** A single rule `{ date: '10-31', time: 18, style: 'party' }` applies `party` all day before 18:00 because `evaluateTimeMatches` wraps around when no other rules exist for that date.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Modify `evaluateTimeMatches`: if time is before the earliest specified rule on that date/range and no midnight rule exists, return `null` so lower-priority time rules or fallback can apply.
  - [x] Update tests to verify expected date+time scoping.

---

### [x] T06: Add `"use client";` Directive to `@omid2007hope/autotheme/react`

- **Files:** [`src/react/useAutoTheme.js:1`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/react/useAutoTheme.js#L1), [`package.json:25`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/package.json#L25)
- **Problem:** Next.js App Router and React Server Components (RSC) error on import without a `"use client";` boundary banner.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Add `"use client";` at top of `src/react/useAutoTheme.js`.
  - [x] Configure `tsup` build banner (`--banner.js '"use client";'`) for the React entry point.

---

### [ ] T07: Resolve SSR Hydration Mismatch & Reconcile README

- **Files:** [`README.md:258-264`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/README.md#L258-L264), [`tests/ssr-rendering.test.js:13-22`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/tests/ssr-rendering.test.js#L13-L22), [`src/react/useAutoTheme.js:59`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/react/useAutoTheme.js#L59)
- **Problem:** README claims server returns fallback; code evaluates server time. In `useAutoTheme()`, `useState(() => evaluate())` runs on server, causing client hydration mismatch when server and client clocks/timezones differ.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Align `useAutoTheme()` hydration: render fallback on initial SSR mount, then seamlessly sync active theme client-side.
  - [x] Reconcile `README.md` and `ssr-rendering.test.js` to define exact, unified SSR behavior.

---

## 🟡 P2 — Medium (Architecture Duplication, Performance & Leaks)

### [ ] T08: Eliminate `JSON.stringify` on Every Component Render

- **Files:** [`src/react/useAutoTheme.js:41-50`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/react/useAutoTheme.js#L41-L50)
- **Problem:** `JSON.stringify(rules)` runs up to twice per render cycle, creating CPU lag on large rule sets (e.g. 1440-rule minute resolution).
- **Action Plan:**
  - [x] Replace naive `JSON.stringify` with shallow array comparison or accept pre-compiled rules directly.

---

### [ ] T09: Deduplicate Rule Evaluation Logic in `css-vars.js`

- **Files:** [`src/adapters/css-vars.js:50-90`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/adapters/css-vars.js#L50-L90), [`src/core/engine.js:186-230`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/autotheme/src/core/engine.js#L186-L230)
- **Problem:** ~40 lines of rule matching and priority resolution are copy-pasted between `engine.js` and `css-vars.js`.
- **Action Plan:**
  - [ ] Extract `resolveRule(compiled, now)` in `engine.js` and import it in `css-vars.js`.

